1
00:01:07,768 --> 00:01:09,862
<i>Now switching to local news,</i>

2
00:01:10,037 --> 00:01:13,303
<i>live from the Fulton
County Court House.</i>

3
00:01:13,473 --> 00:01:16,204
<i>Miss Mclntyre. Can
we get a comment?</i>

4
00:01:16,376 --> 00:01:18,072
<i>Were you surprised
with the jury's verdict?</i>

5
00:01:18,245 --> 00:01:20,441
<i>I'm never surprised
at an acquittal.</i>

6
00:01:20,614 --> 00:01:22,774
<i>And if you believe that,
there's a bridge north of here</i>

7
00:01:22,916 --> 00:01:24,942
<i>you might be
interested in buying.</i>

8
00:01:33,493 --> 00:01:35,689
Hey, Kevin.

9
00:01:35,862 --> 00:01:37,421
Hello.

10
00:01:45,072 --> 00:01:46,335
Donuts get a bad rap.

11
00:01:46,506 --> 00:01:49,635
Yeah, Greg, donuts are a
terribly misunderstood health food.

12
00:01:49,810 --> 00:01:52,336
Look here, here's
your basic jelly donut.

13
00:01:52,512 --> 00:01:55,141
Here's your fruit. Everybody
knows that fruit's good for you.

14
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:57,807
It's got your carbos.
You got to have carbos.

15
00:02:00,053 --> 00:02:01,544
Mm, mm.

16
00:02:03,490 --> 00:02:04,958
Who's the babe?

17
00:02:05,125 --> 00:02:06,718
Some woman I saw the other day.

18
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:08,725
Lawyer. GREG: Pretty face.

19
00:02:08,895 --> 00:02:11,091
- How's the rest of her?
- Good.

20
00:02:11,264 --> 00:02:13,995
She works out four mornings a
week and at nights when she can.

21
00:02:14,167 --> 00:02:16,261
- You dating her?
- No.

22
00:02:16,436 --> 00:02:17,460
You know her?

23
00:02:19,740 --> 00:02:20,764
Not yet.

24
00:02:21,508 --> 00:02:23,943
There's a small matter
we need to discuss.

25
00:02:24,578 --> 00:02:28,606
You didn't speak to Matthew Lyons.
He is now three weeks late on 200K.

26
00:02:30,617 --> 00:02:33,451
He's paid us before.
Give him some slack.

27
00:02:33,620 --> 00:02:35,816
Our employer is impatient.
He'd like you to make that

28
00:02:35,989 --> 00:02:38,220
eminently clear to Mr. Lyons.

29
00:02:40,227 --> 00:02:41,695
I want out, Greg.

30
00:02:42,596 --> 00:02:45,156
You want out. The
boss won't like it.

31
00:02:45,332 --> 00:02:49,064
What about the 150,000
a year you make tax-free?

32
00:02:49,236 --> 00:02:51,865
And this house. How
you gonna rent it?

33
00:02:52,039 --> 00:02:55,532
I can do without it. And
I'll take care of Mr. Lyons.

34
00:02:56,043 --> 00:02:59,946
A couple of days.
This is the last one.

35
00:03:00,914 --> 00:03:03,816
Fine. Just do it soon.

36
00:06:06,700 --> 00:06:10,432
How much it set
you back at that gym?

37
00:06:10,604 --> 00:06:13,631
- Fifty dollars a month.
- Fifty dollars a month?

38
00:06:14,808 --> 00:06:16,709
That's about a
dollar-and-a-half a day.

39
00:06:16,877 --> 00:06:19,176
You spend more than
that on a hot dog at lunch.

40
00:06:19,346 --> 00:06:21,872
Fifty dollars a month. Whew.

41
00:06:24,217 --> 00:06:26,686
- Dad, I came to ask you a favor.
- What?

42
00:06:27,821 --> 00:06:30,916
If you don't mind, I would love
