55
00:07:14,134 --> 00:07:16,865
You've been wearing
the same suit for 20 years.

56
00:07:17,537 --> 00:07:19,403
I like my suit. Fits me perfect.

57
00:07:19,572 --> 00:07:21,268
I know, all seven of them.

58
00:07:22,842 --> 00:07:25,812
Dad, don't you think
it's time for a change?

59
00:07:25,979 --> 00:07:27,140
No.

60
00:07:28,348 --> 00:07:29,748
That suit is outdated.

61
00:07:29,916 --> 00:07:34,980
You are so much more energetic
and vibrant than that suit gives off.

62
00:07:35,155 --> 00:07:36,179
No. I'm not.

63
00:07:36,356 --> 00:07:38,188
Come on, Dad. Let
me take you shopping.

64
00:07:38,358 --> 00:07:41,351
- Please. We'll buy you a new suit.
- I hate to go shopping.

65
00:07:42,429 --> 00:07:45,228
And they don't make
suits like mine anymore.

66
00:07:46,533 --> 00:07:47,865
No argument there.

67
00:10:14,747 --> 00:10:17,683
Yes. I'd like to report
a robbery, please.

68
00:10:29,462 --> 00:10:30,623
Leanne!

69
00:10:31,397 --> 00:10:32,763
Here, Pop.

70
00:10:32,932 --> 00:10:34,366
Leanne.

71
00:10:35,835 --> 00:10:38,202
- Pop.
- Oh. Are you all right?

72
00:10:38,371 --> 00:10:42,536
Yeah. They took my jewelry and that
silver frame with the picture of us in it.

73
00:10:42,709 --> 00:10:45,042
- That's okay.
- No, it's not.

74
00:10:45,211 --> 00:10:49,171
Ben, listen, who knows,
maybe we'll get lucky.

75
00:10:49,349 --> 00:10:50,749
Great.

76
00:10:51,618 --> 00:10:53,086
Stay at my house tonight.

77
00:10:53,253 --> 00:10:55,654
I'll let you run up and
down the stairs free.

78
00:10:55,822 --> 00:10:58,656
I'll be okay, Dad, they're
not going to come back.

79
00:10:58,825 --> 00:11:02,990
Before I go, would you take one last
look at this inventory of things taken?

80
00:11:04,931 --> 00:11:06,331
Yeah, I think that's it.

81
00:11:16,776 --> 00:11:18,711
<i>March fourth.</i>

82
00:11:18,878 --> 00:11:22,280
<i>I read a poem today by a
poet named James Kavanaugh.</i>

83
00:11:22,448 --> 00:11:24,076
<i>It was about friendship.</i>

84
00:11:25,084 --> 00:11:27,918
<i>There was a passage in
it that really touched me.</i>

85
00:11:29,455 --> 00:11:30,889
<i>"Will you be my friend?</i>

86
00:11:31,624 --> 00:11:33,422
<i>A friend</i>

87
00:11:33,593 --> 00:11:36,859
<i>Who far beyond the
feebleness Of any vow or tie</i>

88
00:11:37,030 --> 00:11:40,467
<i>Will touch the secret
place Where I am really I</i>

89
00:11:41,167 --> 00:11:45,002
<i>To know the pain of lips
that plead And eyes that weep</i>

90
00:11:45,638 --> 00:11:48,267
<i>Who will not run away
When you find me in the street</i>

91
00:11:49,909 --> 00:11:51,400
<i>Will you be my friend?</i>

92
00:12:05,525 --> 00:12:09,053
The police didn't find any cash
in the defendant's possession

93
00:12:09,229 --> 00:12:11,164
when they searched his car.

94
00:12:11,331 --> 00:12:16,599
The defendant's fingerprints were
not found in the Crestmoor Bank.

95
00:12:16,769 --> 00:12:21,400
In fact, there is not one
shred of forensic evidence

96
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:26,911
that places the defendant
anywhere near the Crestmoor Bank

97
00:12:27,080 --> 00:12:29,049
on the night of the robbery.

98
00:12:29,215 --> 00:12:31,480
So I have to ask you:

99
00:12:31,651 --> 00:12:38,182
Is there reasonable doubt that
the defendant committed this crime?

100
00:12:40,126 --> 00:12:42,027
I think there's plenty of it.

101
00:12:45,598 --> 00:12:48,693
Ladies and gentlemen of the
jury, it is now time for the judge

102
00:12:48,868 --> 00:12:51,394
to instruct you in the law
that applies to this case.

103
00:12:55,775 --> 00:12:57,971
Who taught you how to
give a closing argument?

104
00:12:58,144 --> 00:13:01,637
- You did.
- No wonder I liked it so much.

105
00:13:01,814 --> 00:13:04,147
Leanne Mclntyre, Kevin Gilliam.

106
00:13:05,118 --> 00:13:06,984
I'm sorry. Do we
know each other?

107
00:13:07,153 --> 00:13:09,498
Did you get the message I left on
your answering machine at home?

108
00:13:09,522 --> 00:13:13,050
No, I didn't. And if you're looking for
an attorney, now isn't a good time...

109
00:13:13,226 --> 00:13:17,095
No, no. I'm a writer. I'm doing an
article for <i>Georgia Today</i> magazine

110
00:13:17,263 --> 00:13:19,061
called <i>Women In The Courtroom.</i>

111
00:13:19,232 --> 00:13:22,794
I'm profiling some of Atlanta's
prominent female attorneys,

112
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:26,064
and I was hoping you'd
let me interview you.

113
00:13:26,239 --> 00:13:27,901
<i>Georgia Today.</i>

114
00:13:28,474 --> 00:13:29,908
- Mister...?
- Gilliam.

115
00:13:30,076 --> 00:13:33,171
What I was about to say,
Mr. Gilliam, is this isn't a good time

116
00:13:33,346 --> 00:13:35,781
for me to commit to anything
right now. I'm very busy.

117
00:13:35,948 --> 00:13:38,645
No problem. Why don't I
call you in a day or two?

118
00:13:38,818 --> 00:13:41,287
- Maybe things will have eased up.
- That'll be fine.

119
00:13:41,454 --> 00:13:44,219
- Okay. It was nice meeting you both.
- Nice meeting you.

120
00:13:46,526 --> 00:13:49,291
<i>Georgia Today.</i>
That's top drawer.

121
00:13:49,462 --> 00:13:51,124
We'll see, Pop.

122
00:13:53,766 --> 00:13:57,362
- Wanna go shopping?
- You wanna go shopping?

123
00:13:57,537 --> 00:14:01,975
Well, I found a silver picture
frame like that one that was taken,

124
00:14:02,141 --> 00:14:05,270
