193
00:18:48,694 --> 00:18:51,061
You know, I probably
should have postponed this.

194
00:18:52,098 --> 00:18:54,329
Do you always get this
upset when you lose?

195
00:18:54,500 --> 00:18:57,129
Only when I'm sure
my client didn't do it.

196
00:18:59,205 --> 00:19:01,868
- You really care, don't you?
- Yeah.

197
00:19:03,643 --> 00:19:06,169
Has anyone ever told you
you have beautiful skin?

198
00:19:07,380 --> 00:19:08,404
Thank you.

199
00:19:09,215 --> 00:19:10,843
Great eyes.

200
00:19:12,385 --> 00:19:15,253
It must be difficult for you
to have much of a social life

201
00:19:15,421 --> 00:19:17,481
with the heavy work
schedule you keep.

202
00:19:18,557 --> 00:19:21,584
Well, I make time for the
things that are important to me.

203
00:19:22,328 --> 00:19:24,729
Does that mean you're
dating anyone regularly?

204
00:19:27,033 --> 00:19:29,901
Are you doing an
article on me as a lawyer,

205
00:19:30,069 --> 00:19:32,868
- or are you coming on to me?
- It was just a question.

206
00:19:33,039 --> 00:19:35,474
No. It wasn't just a
question. It was a pass.

207
00:19:36,342 --> 00:19:39,073
And I really don't appreciate you
misrepresenting yourself to me.

208
00:19:39,245 --> 00:19:41,605
- Leanne, I wasn't coming on to you.
- You know what, Kevin,

209
00:19:41,747 --> 00:19:45,309
the interview is
over. Enjoy the torte.

210
00:20:17,750 --> 00:20:20,049
So where have you been all day?

211
00:20:20,219 --> 00:20:21,744
Catching up on some errands.

212
00:20:22,621 --> 00:20:24,351
Nice threads.

213
00:20:25,925 --> 00:20:28,895
Cologne. Have a
hot date, my man?

214
00:20:29,595 --> 00:20:31,587
Yeah, I had a date. Kind of.

215
00:20:31,764 --> 00:20:34,097
Why do I feel like
you're wasting your time?

216
00:20:38,204 --> 00:20:39,399
You're writing your memoirs.

217
00:20:40,339 --> 00:20:41,671
I stole her diary.

218
00:20:41,841 --> 00:20:43,309
You're not a burglar.

219
00:20:44,376 --> 00:20:46,743
I want to know everything
I can about Leanne.

220
00:20:46,912 --> 00:20:49,313
- Leanne?
- Yes. Mclntyre.

221
00:20:49,482 --> 00:20:52,418
Why do you want to know so
much about Leanne Mclntyre?

222
00:20:54,220 --> 00:20:55,654
It's important to me.

223
00:20:57,323 --> 00:20:59,656
How's Mr. Lyons feeling?

224
00:21:00,559 --> 00:21:02,152
I haven't done it.

225
00:21:03,362 --> 00:21:04,955
I know.

226
00:21:05,131 --> 00:21:07,600
I told you I would do
it this one last time.

227
00:21:07,767 --> 00:21:11,169
You tell the boss
I want to be clean.

228
00:21:12,705 --> 00:21:14,401
Forget the girl, Kev.

229
00:21:17,309 --> 00:21:20,211
And don't bite the
hand that feeds you.

230
00:21:43,302 --> 00:21:44,668
Mr. Lyons.

231
00:21:46,906 --> 00:21:48,602
I'll have it all in 48
hours. No problem.

232
00:21:48,774 --> 00:21:50,242
I promise.

233
00:21:51,610 --> 00:21:54,978
You give me half of it now,
maybe it could buy you some time.

234
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:56,672
Tell him I'll have
the money Thursday.

235
00:22:02,288 --> 00:22:04,052
I don't want to hurt you.

236
00:22:04,223 --> 00:22:06,454
I don't have it, Kevin. Please.

237
00:22:06,625 --> 00:22:08,218
I gotta break something.

238
00:22:10,029 --> 00:22:11,588
Don't.

239
00:22:11,764 --> 00:22:15,326
- I got my orders, I'm sorry.
- I'll have the money in 48 hours.

240
00:22:44,897 --> 00:22:46,525
Can we start this over again?

241
00:22:47,233 --> 00:22:49,327
I hated what happened today.

242
00:22:50,636 --> 00:22:52,901
- This really isn't necessary.
- Yes, it is.

243
00:22:53,072 --> 00:22:55,166
Because I was coming on to you.

244
00:22:55,941 --> 00:22:59,275
I guess I was just overwhelmed
with this attraction I was feeling for you

245
00:22:59,445 --> 00:23:03,541
and, ahem, heh, I
responded badly.

246
00:23:05,718 --> 00:23:07,448
Would you like to come in?

247
00:23:08,754 --> 00:23:10,245
Thank you.

248
00:23:19,999 --> 00:23:21,797
If I'd known I was
going to upset you...

249
00:23:21,967 --> 00:23:23,196
No. It was just bad timing.

250
00:23:24,436 --> 00:23:26,769
And I probably overreacted too.

251
00:23:28,307 --> 00:23:30,105
It's just been a
rough couple of days.

252
00:23:31,710 --> 00:23:33,838
Something you can talk about?

253
00:23:35,247 --> 00:23:36,545
Want to sit down?

254
00:23:38,651 --> 00:23:41,086
My place was
burglarized the other day.

255
00:23:41,620 --> 00:23:42,952
Oh, um...

256
00:23:43,122 --> 00:23:45,887
- I'm sorry.
- The insurance will reimburse me.

257
00:23:46,058 --> 00:23:47,686
Mostly took costume jewelry.

258
00:23:47,860 --> 00:23:51,126
Nothing worth much except for a
couple of pieces my mom gave me.

259
00:23:51,297 --> 00:23:53,391
And those I'll never replace.

260
00:23:54,266 --> 00:23:58,567
And then last night, I discovered
that my diary was gone.

261
00:23:59,605 --> 00:24:02,598
- You think it was stolen?
- Well, it's missing.

262
00:24:02,775 --> 00:24:04,710
I keep it in that
drawer every night.

263
00:24:06,845 --> 00:24:08,438
Anyway, enough about that.

264
00:24:14,386 --> 00:24:17,015
Looks like a book.
Shall I open it?

265
00:24:17,189 --> 00:24:20,216
Absolutely. It's one
of my favorite poets.

266
00:24:27,199 --> 00:24:29,998
- James Kavanaugh.
- You've heard of him?

267
00:24:30,169 --> 00:24:31,169
Oh!

268
00:24:31,337 --> 00:24:34,432
I love this man's work. I
can't believe you know him.

269
00:24:35,674 --> 00:24:36,801
Thank you.

270
00:24:36,976 --> 00:24:38,740
You're very welcome.

271
00:24:42,915 --> 00:24:44,042
You want to stay for dinner?

272
00:24:44,216 --> 00:24:46,742
I was just making myself
a salad. It'll feed five.

273
00:24:46,919 --> 00:24:48,751
I have a better idea.

274
00:24:48,921 --> 00:24:50,321
Let me take you out to dinner.

275
00:24:50,489 --> 00:24:54,051
I promise I'll behave, and
we can do the interview.

276
00:24:55,728 --> 00:24:56,991
Okay.

277
00:24:58,397 --> 00:25:01,299
- Let me just go change.
- Take your time.

278
00:25:34,867 --> 00:25:37,632
- Damn it!
- Are you okay?

279
00:25:40,472 --> 00:25:41,770
Leanne?

280
00:25:50,249 --> 00:25:51,808
Is everything all right?

281
00:25:51,984 --> 00:25:53,919
- It's gone.
- What?

282
00:25:54,920 --> 00:25:57,082
My grandmother's brooch.

283
00:25:57,256 --> 00:25:58,747
She gave it to me
on my 16th birthday.

284
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:02,318
I'm sorry.

285
00:26:03,262 --> 00:26:04,958
It was on this jacket.

286
00:26:06,098 --> 00:26:09,466
It was the first piece of jewelry
my grandfather ever bought for her.

287
00:26:18,077 --> 00:26:19,568
Wow.

288
00:26:19,978 --> 00:26:21,844
This guy's really
changed my life.

289
00:26:23,315 --> 00:26:26,717
Changes the way I breathe
when I walk into my own house,

290
00:26:26,885 --> 00:26:29,946
the way I sleep,
the way I think.

291
00:26:35,594 --> 00:26:37,927
What kind of person does this?

292
00:27:01,053 --> 00:27:02,851
Do you think juries
look at you differently

293
00:27:03,021 --> 00:27:04,922
than they do male trial lawyers?

294
00:27:05,090 --> 00:27:06,956
Some do. There's no question.

295
00:27:07,993 --> 00:27:10,827
When my dad is attacking
a witness' testimony,

296
00:27:10,996 --> 00:27:13,192
I love to watch
the jury's faces.

297
00:27:13,365 --> 00:27:17,598
They seem almost
mesmerized sometimes.

298
00:27:18,403 --> 00:27:19,894
I can't act like that.

299
00:27:20,072 --> 00:27:22,667
Juries don't like that kind of
aggressiveness in a woman.

300
00:27:22,841 --> 00:27:24,673
It's not feminine.

301
00:27:24,843 --> 00:27:26,607
I can see that in their faces.

302
00:27:26,778 --> 00:27:28,406
Don't you resent that?

303
00:27:28,580 --> 00:27:31,175
Yes, but I let it go.

304
00:27:32,651 --> 00:27:33,983
You wanna know a secret?

305
00:27:34,987 --> 00:27:36,649
I try to act like my dad.

306
00:27:36,822 --> 00:27:40,782
Sometimes it works, and
sometimes I just can't pull it off.

307
00:27:45,097 --> 00:27:48,966
Okay. So, you must be getting
bored, hearing me go on about myself.

308
00:27:49,134 --> 00:27:50,693
Hardly.

309
00:27:51,637 --> 00:27:54,607
What about you? Did you
always want to be a writer?

310
00:27:56,975 --> 00:28:01,174
No one grows up dreaming of being
a writer for <i>Georgia Today</i> magazine.

311
00:28:01,346 --> 00:28:03,747
Okay. So, what did you
want to be when you grew up?

312
00:28:03,916 --> 00:28:05,350
You won't laugh?

313
00:28:06,985 --> 00:28:09,955
- An actor.
- Are you serious?

314
00:28:10,122 --> 00:28:11,454
You didn't see <i>Phantom?</i>

315
00:28:11,657 --> 00:28:13,649
You were in <i>Phantom
of the Opera?</i>

316
00:28:13,825 --> 00:28:15,225
No.

317
00:28:15,394 --> 00:28:17,329
But I did sing in a
production of <i>The Magic Flute</i>

318
00:28:17,496 --> 00:28:19,328
in Sewickley, Pennsylvania.

319
00:28:35,847 --> 00:28:37,372
What are you smiling about?

320
00:28:37,549 --> 00:28:40,314
- Gonna do it again.
- Do what?

321
00:28:40,485 --> 00:28:42,954
I can't believe this. I
feel like a school kid.

322
00:28:43,689 --> 00:28:45,180
I wanted to hold your hand.

323
00:29:07,980 --> 00:29:11,473
- Mr. Lyons squared up today.
- Good.

324
00:29:13,418 --> 00:29:16,320
I told you I'd take care of
Mr. Lyons, and I did that.

325
00:29:16,488 --> 00:29:18,855
- Now I'm through.
- What the hell's wrong with you?

326
00:29:19,024 --> 00:29:20,959
- Are you nuts?
- Maybe.

327
00:29:21,126 --> 00:29:22,651
You're a thug, Kevin.

328
00:29:22,828 --> 00:29:24,868
She's a lawyer, a lawyer
whose house you ripped off.

329
00:29:25,030 --> 00:29:26,896
Do you think you're
gonna marry her now?

330
00:29:28,867 --> 00:29:31,962
No. Consider me retired.

331
00:29:33,005 --> 00:29:35,167
Giving up the business,
are we? Going straight?

332
00:29:35,340 --> 00:29:36,569
Get out of here, Greg.

333
00:29:36,742 --> 00:29:40,645
You made 150K last year, tiger,
what are you gonna do, wait tables?

334
00:29:40,812 --> 00:29:42,542
You need a shrink, man.

335
00:30:04,970 --> 00:30:10,204
Well, I'll see you in a couple
of hours. I got a bail hearing.

336
00:30:10,375 --> 00:30:13,277
I won't be here. I'm going
to meet Kevin at the beach.

337
00:30:13,445 --> 00:30:16,347
Boy, that must be some
long article he's writing.

338
00:30:21,053 --> 00:30:22,612
Where's your new suit?

339
00:30:26,525 --> 00:30:27,686
In my closet.

340
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:32,497
- Why?
- It's where I keep all my new suits.

341
00:30:32,664 --> 00:30:33,893
Dad.

342
00:30:37,869 --> 00:30:40,100
We bought that
suit for a reason.

343
00:30:40,939 --> 00:30:44,171
That's right, to cheer you
up, and you do seem happier.

344
00:30:45,143 --> 00:30:49,046
Go on, Dad. Go on
upstairs and change.

345
00:31:10,369 --> 00:31:13,806
My client is an exemplary
member of this community,

346
00:31:13,972 --> 00:31:19,001
and he has been unjustly
accused of these charges.

347
00:31:19,778 --> 00:31:22,873
- Mr. Matlock.
- Yes, sir?

348
00:31:24,182 --> 00:31:26,344
- Are you all right?
- I'm fine, sir.

349
00:31:26,518 --> 00:31:29,852
You... You look different.

350
00:31:31,523 --> 00:31:34,459
- For the better or the worse?
- Not sure.

351
00:31:35,127 --> 00:31:37,722
I saw you in the hall and
didn't know who you were.

352
00:31:37,896 --> 00:31:39,364
I had to ask somebody.

353
00:31:40,699 --> 00:31:41,997
- Proceed.
- Yes, sir.

354
00:31:42,167 --> 00:31:46,127
Uh, as I was saying, my
client is an exemplary member

355
00:31:46,304 --> 00:31:50,400
of this community and there's
no reason in the world to believe

356
00:31:50,575 --> 00:31:52,043
there's any...

357
00:31:52,978 --> 00:31:54,446
danger of flight.

358
00:31:55,147 --> 00:31:58,515
He has lived in the
same house for 15 years,

359
00:31:58,683 --> 00:32:01,380
held the same job for ten years,

360
00:32:02,220 --> 00:32:07,022
and he's anxious to come into this
court so he can clear his good name.

361
00:32:07,192 --> 00:32:09,093
Excuse me, just a second.

362
00:32:17,736 --> 00:32:21,070
What's the matter with you,
Mr. Matlock? Is something wrong?

363
00:32:21,239 --> 00:32:23,799
Your Honor, can I just
have a ten minute recess?

364
00:32:24,009 --> 00:32:25,602
During a bail hearing?

365
00:32:25,777 --> 00:32:27,817
Five minutes. I'll be right
back before you know it.

366
00:32:27,979 --> 00:32:29,845
All right.

367
00:32:30,015 --> 00:32:33,349
This court will remain
in recess for five minutes.

368
00:32:52,037 --> 00:32:53,037
Oh.

369
00:32:53,205 --> 00:32:56,266
Yeah, that's why I didn't
know you, Mr. Matlock.

370
00:32:56,441 --> 00:32:59,036
- Yes, sir.
- You okay now?

371
00:32:59,211 --> 00:33:02,272
All perfect, just
like my old self.

372
00:33:03,448 --> 00:33:04,814
As I was saying...

373
00:33:06,618 --> 00:33:08,610
I'll give you five dollars
if we can stop running.

374
00:33:08,787 --> 00:33:11,120
Come on, 5O more
yards, big finish, let's go.

375
00:33:12,224 --> 00:33:13,852
Come on.

376
00:33:16,394 --> 00:33:18,920
I gotta stop. You're killing me.

377
00:33:19,798 --> 00:33:21,926
Tell me you thought
that was exhilarating.

378
00:33:22,100 --> 00:33:25,264
That was exhausting. I
gotta get something to drink.

379
00:33:26,638 --> 00:33:29,130
Come on, we'll call the
paramedics from over there.

380
00:33:29,307 --> 00:33:31,606
I'll race you. Come on.

381
00:33:33,445 --> 00:33:34,622
- Hello.
- Two, please.

382
00:33:34,646 --> 00:33:35,875
This way.

383
00:33:44,222 --> 00:33:46,862
We gotta get out of here. He's
one of the biggest bores I ever met.

384
00:33:47,025 --> 00:33:49,551
- If we sit, he'll never leave us alone.
- All right.

385
00:33:50,395 --> 00:33:51,988
Thanks, anyway.

386
00:34:08,246 --> 00:34:10,681
- Is something wrong?
- No.

387
00:34:11,283 --> 00:34:14,720
You were so quiet at dinner.
You seemed sort of sad.

388
00:34:14,886 --> 00:34:16,582
I'm sorry.

389
00:34:16,755 --> 00:34:19,355
Maybe it's the realization that my
dreams of winning the decathlon

390
00:34:19,524 --> 00:34:21,288
were shattered
today on that beach.

391
00:34:39,744 --> 00:34:42,839
- Wanna come in?
- I should go. It's late.

392
00:34:43,481 --> 00:34:45,973
Cup of decaf? We
could talk a while.

393
00:34:46,151 --> 00:34:49,644
- About what?
- This and that.

394
00:34:51,256 --> 00:34:53,350
This and that
can take all night.

395
00:35:00,665 --> 00:35:04,625
- What's wrong?
- It's complicated.

396
00:35:05,270 --> 00:35:06,294
Are you married?

397
00:35:07,973 --> 00:35:10,033
If it were only that simple.

398
00:35:10,208 --> 00:35:12,177
Well, what is it?

399
00:35:14,279 --> 00:35:16,748
This wasn't a
good idea. I'm sorry.

400
00:36:49,140 --> 00:36:50,836
- Pop.
- Hi.

401
00:36:51,009 --> 00:36:52,409
How was dinner last night?

402
00:36:53,645 --> 00:36:55,365
I'm gonna save you a
whole lot of questions.

403
00:36:55,513 --> 00:36:57,393
I don't think I'm gonna
be seeing Kevin anymore.

404
00:36:57,549 --> 00:36:59,211
What happened?

405
00:36:59,784 --> 00:37:01,218
Well...

406
00:37:02,654 --> 00:37:04,282
What are you doing?

407
00:37:05,056 --> 00:37:07,651
Um, I'm, uh... I'm
taking a suit back.

408
00:37:08,526 --> 00:37:09,550
Why?

409
00:37:11,563 --> 00:37:14,533
- It didn't work out.
- It didn't work out?

410
00:37:14,699 --> 00:37:17,794
What does that
mean? Doesn't fit?

411
00:37:17,969 --> 00:37:21,770
It fits. It just doesn't fit me.

412
00:37:21,940 --> 00:37:24,171
- You can't take it back.
- I only wore it once.

413
00:37:24,342 --> 00:37:25,742
They altered it.

414
00:37:25,910 --> 00:37:27,845
I'll rip out the stitches.

415
00:37:28,012 --> 00:37:29,173
It'll be like new.

416
00:37:30,181 --> 00:37:31,376
I bought you something.

417
00:37:32,117 --> 00:37:34,086
- What's this for?
- Nothing. Just...

418
00:37:37,489 --> 00:37:41,187
Oh, Dad, you didn't have
to replace the picture frame.

419
00:37:41,359 --> 00:37:43,794
I know you didn't want
to start replacing things.

420
00:37:43,962 --> 00:37:45,658
But I just thought...

421
00:37:47,499 --> 00:37:49,058
Thank you.

422
00:38:25,837 --> 00:38:27,669
Well, what do you know?

423
00:38:52,931 --> 00:38:56,390
<i>I read a poem today by a
poet named James Kavanaugh.</i>

424
00:38:56,568 --> 00:38:58,400
<i>It was about friendship.</i>

425
00:39:05,977 --> 00:39:08,503
Looks like a book.
Shall I open it?

426
00:39:08,680 --> 00:39:12,811
Absolutely. He's one
of my favorite poets.

427
00:39:15,520 --> 00:39:19,321
- James Kavanaugh.
- You've heard of him?

428
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:22,892
I love this man's work. I
can't believe you know him.

429
00:39:34,939 --> 00:39:37,738
<i>Bundled up in Grandma's
comforter, drinking hot chocolate,</i>

430
00:39:37,909 --> 00:39:40,743
<i>eating my homemade Linzer torte.</i>

431
00:39:44,115 --> 00:39:46,315
It's a beautiful day. How
about we meet at Freiman Park?

432
00:39:46,451 --> 00:39:48,171
- Great.
- I'll pick up some pastries.

433
00:39:48,319 --> 00:39:51,380
- Do you like Linzer torte?
- Excuse me?

434
00:39:51,556 --> 00:39:54,355
I was asking you if
you liked Linzer torte.

435
00:40:07,205 --> 00:40:08,935
Are you married?

436
00:40:09,107 --> 00:40:11,542
If it were only that simple.

437
00:40:11,709 --> 00:40:13,268
Well, what is it?

438
00:40:14,913 --> 00:40:16,973
This wasn't a good idea.

439
00:40:17,148 --> 00:40:18,377
I'm sorry.

440
00:40:38,169 --> 00:40:42,402
Yes, please, could I have the
number of <i>Georgia Today</i> magazine?

441
00:41:50,041 --> 00:41:52,101
What the hell? Gee.

442
00:41:52,410 --> 00:41:53,708
Leanne.

443
00:42:02,020 --> 00:42:03,716
I want my jewelry back.

444
00:42:05,523 --> 00:42:10,120
You're very good. Make a date with me
at the park, so you can follow me here.

445
00:42:10,294 --> 00:42:12,195
That's a side of you I
would never have guessed.

446
00:42:12,363 --> 00:42:14,730
Maybe if you'd read my entire
diary, this wouldn't have come

447
00:42:14,899 --> 00:42:16,424
as such a surprise to you.

448
00:42:16,601 --> 00:42:18,331
I never read your diary.

449
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:22,738
I must have gone through that
drawer a dozen times looking for it.

450
00:42:24,442 --> 00:42:25,740
Tell me something.

451
00:42:27,345 --> 00:42:30,179
Did you use the key that I hide
outside the door to put it back?

452
00:42:32,950 --> 00:42:37,445
I wanted to mention to you I
called <i>Georgia Today</i> magazine.

453
00:42:38,790 --> 00:42:40,656
Nobody there has
ever heard of you.

454
00:42:40,825 --> 00:42:43,106
I'm not surprised. I'm writing
the article on speculation.

455
00:42:46,264 --> 00:42:47,755
You're a liar.

456
00:42:49,834 --> 00:42:51,632
I went back to that
cafe at the beach,

457
00:42:51,803 --> 00:42:54,170
found out who the man
was with the broken hand.

458
00:42:55,173 --> 00:42:56,971
How do you live with yourself?

459
00:43:02,146 --> 00:43:03,637
Leanne.

460
00:43:03,815 --> 00:43:07,877
Let me just... Let me just
make sure I've got this straight.

461
00:43:09,587 --> 00:43:13,854
In your off hours, you
break into women's homes,

462
00:43:14,025 --> 00:43:19,293
rip off their diaries, and then try to
become the man you think they want?

463
00:43:20,865 --> 00:43:22,663
That's completely
untrue, Leanne.

464
00:43:26,170 --> 00:43:27,502
Leanne.

465
00:43:52,396 --> 00:43:54,126
When were you
gonna give this to me?

466
00:43:55,399 --> 00:43:56,492
Excuse me?

467
00:43:56,667 --> 00:44:00,832
You know damn well I wrote about
lingerie from Tattinger's in my diary.

468
00:44:03,341 --> 00:44:05,606
When were you
gonna give this to me?

469
00:44:09,313 --> 00:44:11,441
Well, I...

470
00:44:13,985 --> 00:44:16,045
I'm coming after you.

471
00:44:16,220 --> 00:44:19,054
I don't care how
long it takes me.

472
00:44:19,223 --> 00:44:22,159
I'm gonna get you for
breaking into my home.

473
00:44:23,327 --> 00:44:25,057
- Leanne.
- Oh.

474
00:44:26,097 --> 00:44:28,293
Your concern overwhelms me.

475
00:44:32,637 --> 00:44:35,300
It was all just a game
for you, wasn't it?

476
00:44:37,108 --> 00:44:40,476
Leanne, Leanne.

477
00:44:42,647 --> 00:44:44,707
Before you go, think about this.

478
00:44:46,851 --> 00:44:49,650
If it was just a game, why
didn't I spend the night with you?

479
00:44:50,621 --> 00:44:53,181
Remember, "talking
about this and that"?

480
00:44:55,459 --> 00:44:57,360
I could have, you know.

481
00:45:45,943 --> 00:45:48,105
- Hi.
- Hi, Dad.

482
00:45:49,313 --> 00:45:51,373
I thought you might be here.

483
00:45:51,949 --> 00:45:54,976
- How you doing?
- I'll be okay.

484
00:45:58,256 --> 00:46:03,388
I found something of yours
this morning at my house.

485
00:46:08,065 --> 00:46:11,229
Grandma's brooch.
Where did you find it?

486
00:46:11,402 --> 00:46:15,066
